#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105467 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e475613-ff86-5655-a966-121d622b0bd7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Interior Angles of a Regular Polygon"}] :question/id #uuid "f617d0de-cdcb-5d15-aa91-1d3e6f5edb60" :question/math-academy-id "e-12627" :question/problem "![](images/83/830bc07f05846dcb09e360d6863387c9cc51eddc0027fe153cb2217cf7263a5a.png)\n\nThe hexagon $ABCDEF$ is regular. Find the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "A regular hexagon is a $6$-sided polygon where all the interior angles have the same measure.\n\nThe sum of the measures of its interior angles is \n\n$$\n180^\\circ \\times (6 - 2) = 720^\\circ.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the measure of  $\\angle BAF$  is \n\n$$\nm\\angle BAF  = \\dfrac{720^\\circ}{6} = 120^\\circ.\n$$\n\nThe angles $\\angle QAB,$ $\\angle BAF,$ and $\\angle FAP$ form a straight angle. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠QAB+m∠BAF+m∠FAP & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ x+m∠BAF+x & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 2x+{120}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105468 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105698 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5231e20f-0e57-517c-bae9-3a152234d5ab" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Exterior Angles of a Regular Polygon"}] :question/id #uuid "2fff10bc-b4a2-5f6c-b1a2-2fa2c5510f60" :question/math-academy-id "e-12628" :question/problem "In a regular polygon, all the exterior angles have a measure of $20^\\circ.$ How many sides does the polygon have?" :question/worked-solution "The sum of the exterior angles of any polygon is $360^\\circ.$ \n\nFor a regular polygon, all exterior angles have the same measure. \n\nTherefore, the number of exterior angles is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{360^\\circ}{20^\\circ} = 18\\,.\n$$\n\nThe number of sides, then, is also $18.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105469 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "372bcfad-79d0-5758-a66b-efeacfb13762" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exterior Angles With Multiple Polygons"}] :question/id #uuid "97bdacef-ecd4-52da-9fef-b8e9233f21a8" :question/math-academy-id "e-12629" :question/problem "The diagram shows a regular octagon and a regular triangle. Find the measure of the shaded angle.\n\n![](images/18/18698bc2682a34c6d5c85038b8a54ae78f85605b336a78a6875e0cfd712009c6.png)" :question/worked-solution "The shaded angle is the sum of the measures of exterior angles of a regular octagon and a regular triangle.\n\n![](images/04/04684884166fb5b87434b078962c78f71df65a0898e94c247b2763c6ba1368a3.png)\n\nFor any polygon, the exterior angles sum to $360^\\circ.$ In a regular octagon, there are $8$ equivalent exterior angles, so each has a measure of \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{360^\\circ}{8} = 45^\\circ .\n$$\n\nLikewise, in a regular triangle, there are $3$ equivalent exterior angles, so each has a measure of \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{360^\\circ}{3} = 120^\\circ .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the given angle has the following measure:\n\n$$\n45^\\circ + 120^\\circ = 165^\\circ\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105470 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105696 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9f78a76-4d2f-5694-971c-e734bc330602" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Regular Polygons"}] :question/id #uuid "fbeb62a5-1a2c-53df-ab8d-6aaee87c4a11" :question/math-academy-id "e-12647" :question/problem "Which of the shapes below is a regular polygon?\n\n![](images/40/403ae7e178e17d08d44bebd17b53e0831d30eb0be0ad25d1710a289d2400400e.png)" :question/worked-solution "A regular polygon is a polygon that has the following properties:\n\n- All sides have the same length (i.e., congruent).\n\n- All angles have the same measure (i.e., congruent).\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each polygon in turn:\n\n- Polygon I is regular. Its sides and angles are all congruent.\n\n- Polygon II is regular. Its sides and angles are all congruent.\n\n- Polygon III is not regular. Its sides and angles are *not* all congruent.\n\nTherefore the answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507495 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "372bcfad-79d0-5758-a66b-efeacfb13762" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exterior Angles With Multiple Polygons"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "182da991-9f99-5a4b-bfa2-0cca9c780694" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{114}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506723} {:answer/id #uuid "984c64bb-89ea-53e0-b496-db0e8a029c05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{117}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507009} {:answer/id #uuid "b4ed09aa-f116-526f-b8ba-f798090044f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{121}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507076} {:answer/id #uuid "bbb63712-1a41-5baa-b3f0-135265da0d4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{111}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507090} {:answer/id #uuid "d5896b52-1781-59f9-a592-6c35189aea77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{135}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "984c64bb-89ea-53e0-b496-db0e8a029c05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{117}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507009} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a1140f9-f491-5cea-b921-793b793b375b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507255}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c3f09552-d68e-5579-9dba-5af2d86586af" :question/math-academy-id "q-118720" :question/problem "![](images/dd/dd3401de484cfd0cb096c812d3f7540c31373116ed21b32bc9856b96c4b2ada3.png)\n\nThe diagram shows a regular pentagon and a regular octagon. Find the measure of the shaded angle." :question/worked-solution "The shaded angle is the sum of the measures of exterior angles of a regular pentagon and a regular octagon.\n\n![](images/cd/cd6a3ba04cc8f3f301b6db6a825854ba260cd5ce5b0582b64431f80c78cb7771.png)\n\nFor any polygon, the exterior angles sum up to ${360}^{∘}.$ In a regular pentagon, there are $5$ equivalent exterior angles, so each has a measure of \n\n$$\n\\frac{{360}^{∘}}{5}={72}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, in a regular octagon, there are $8$ equivalent exterior angles, so each has a measure of \n\n$$\n\\frac{{360}^{∘}}{8}={45}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the given angle has the following measure:\n\n$$\n{72}^{∘}+{45}^{∘}={117}^{∘}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507500 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "372bcfad-79d0-5758-a66b-efeacfb13762" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exterior Angles With Multiple Polygons"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52bcd67d-2ecb-5fba-9554-690fda0c2de9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{63}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506868} {:answer/id #uuid "55674318-a23f-5ad4-a960-9e3ae7f6e269" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{61}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506877} {:answer/id #uuid "951c6039-0f9b-5b28-9f7a-bbd52249f3ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{57}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507003} {:answer/id #uuid "aa7a9ac8-ea29-5914-b73b-c547dd962e7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{55}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507056} {:answer/id #uuid "e544e675-b65a-502f-836c-1755a6b03159" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{52}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507179}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "951c6039-0f9b-5b28-9f7a-bbd52249f3ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{57}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507003} :answer-field/id #uuid "850acc0e-411d-5578-8536-830509c75c7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507319}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c8f5c562-09c2-5702-8f52-e246f997c6e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-118734" :question/problem "![](images/45/45a75f709f4a1eb10ac610b25b38689339b00e1b8e08af54486517a1c3a9084d.png)\n\nThe diagram shows an equilateral triangle, a regular pentagon, and a regular octagon. Find the measure of the shaded angle." :question/worked-solution "Note, that the full angle is the sum of the measure of interior angles of an equilateral triangle, a regular octagon, a regular pentagon, and the measure of the shaded angle.\n\n![](images/12/1289ebe280e4fc07cc71a7f45a8660c6ce29fb367567f07e1efb4d3712cbe767.png)\n\n \n\nFor a regular polygon with $n$ sides, the  measure of each interior angle must be\n\n$$\n\\frac{{180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2)}{n}.\n$$\n\n \n\n In an equilateral triangle, there are $3$ equivalent interior angles, so each has a measure of \n\n$$\n\\frac{{180}^{∘}(3-2)}{3}={60}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, in a regular octagon, there are $8$ equivalent interior angles, so each has a measure of \n\n$$\n\\frac{{180}^{∘}(8-2)}{8}={135}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nA regular pentagon has $5$ equivalent interior angles, so each has a measure of \n\n$$\n\\frac{{180}^{∘}(5-2)}{5}={108}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nLet us call $x$ the measure of the shaded angle. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{60}^{∘}+{135}^{∘}+{108}^{∘}+x & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ {303}^{∘}+x & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={57}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507464 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105696 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9f78a76-4d2f-5694-971c-e734bc330602" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Regular Polygons"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "291bd849-41b3-58b8-8e49-1c8ed8860dbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506771} {:answer/id #uuid "8eea286e-1dbb-5fb4-adf8-eccd19834f29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506996} {:answer/id #uuid "b6c4c4d4-9ed2-594a-b454-d1a2c20dfe47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507082} {:answer/id #uuid "bd3908bf-e7c0-50d2-a6e7-0a86ecce7b3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507094} {:answer/id #uuid "e8b8c185-08a3-5bbc-acc8-11fa95c29f29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8eea286e-1dbb-5fb4-adf8-eccd19834f29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506996} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6fee783-5160-5bd8-8a9f-74711b997e61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507372}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9c0ea52d-303e-5339-a018-6f127fed4c0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-169186" :question/problem "![](images/e5/e597f15091f753a2f3271a6b69d8af9b187835f0a61d1e5109d4e8f588c59e6c.png)\n\nWhich of the shapes above is a regular polygon?" :question/worked-solution "A regular polygon is a polygon that has the following properties:\n\n- All sides have the same length (i.e., congruent).\n\n- All angles have the same measure (i.e., congruent).\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each polygon in turn:\n\n- Polygon I is not regular. Its sides and angles are *not* all congruent.\n\n- Polygon II is not regular. Its angles are *not* all congruent.\n\n- Polygon III is regular. Its sides and angles are all congruent.\n\nTherefore the answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507524 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105696 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9f78a76-4d2f-5694-971c-e734bc330602" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Regular Polygons"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58d22869-fda1-5ac3-9bd9-dc4ec83fbd3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506884} {:answer/id #uuid "63b45f62-062f-5cfd-ac49-86534559ad1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506916} {:answer/id #uuid "71d23498-ba55-5df6-97ef-20121a7abf7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506939} {:answer/id #uuid "792eba77-96e3-564e-8727-52f9cd962825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506948} {:answer/id #uuid "945d4d19-8ba2-5b63-b1e6-a1bf8cedffce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507001}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71d23498-ba55-5df6-97ef-20121a7abf7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506939} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1a194fb-39d9-575a-9b97-cdad78698c09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507344}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ec3096db-b68c-5e55-b5e7-cfc51203253a" :question/math-academy-id "q-169189" :question/problem "![](images/b7/b7d373c510472102242794bc21b60a6e0c12100213c6e01aac640feb398fc573.png)\n\nWhich of the shapes above is **NOT** a regular polygon?" :question/worked-solution "A regular polygon is a polygon that has the following properties:\n\n- All sides have the same length (i.e., congruent).\n\n- All angles have the same measure (i.e., congruent).\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each polygon in turn:\n\n- Polygon I is regular. Its sides and angles are all congruent.\n\n- Polygon II is *not* regular. Its sides and angles are *not* all congruent.\n\n- Polygon III is regular. Its sides and angles are all congruent.\n\nTherefore the answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234246 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e475613-ff86-5655-a966-121d622b0bd7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Interior Angles of a Regular Polygon"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "410b5ccb-8809-514e-9fe0-e2ed5203fc5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{140}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506829} {:answer/id #uuid "5bc73c9f-bea7-5aa6-8bc5-7b1952d2fc1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{120}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506896} {:answer/id #uuid "698c4404-6fea-5fe6-ab24-fff51f4f7552" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{144}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506927} {:answer/id #uuid "b0da59ef-f0be-57a2-984b-ca9633005cb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{135}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507068} {:answer/id #uuid "dbcbd481-cf23-5d4b-9076-99fc3782fa8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{108}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507155}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0da59ef-f0be-57a2-984b-ca9633005cb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{135}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507068} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f243037-00be-5d58-ad68-28fd2312e252" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507314}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c5f9e95e-441f-5854-8b96-40080ae934e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-67891" :question/problem "![](images/e1/e17bf0ffc492fc1ed22d97e422cf9926bfac01ac765614bbe63b887853d65e2e.png)\n\nDetermine the measure of each interior angle of a regular octagon." :question/worked-solution "A regular octagon is an $8$-sided polygon where all the interior angles have the same measure.\n\nThe sum of the measures of its interior angles is \n\n$$\n{180}^{∘}\\times (8-2)=1\\,{080}^{∘}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the measure of each interior angle is \n\n$$\n\\frac{1\\,{080}^{∘}}{8}={135}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507430 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e475613-ff86-5655-a966-121d622b0bd7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Interior Angles of a Regular Polygon"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19868881-4c3d-5e74-99e5-c9ebc1782f87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{150}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506725} {:answer/id #uuid "2599c014-0b03-5502-8a02-0d8a8d6a630b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{157.5}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506762} {:answer/id #uuid "33ae0346-a3ac-5e2a-9330-5eb676493021" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{160}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506804} {:answer/id #uuid "aa7b44b0-678d-5779-83f2-0a355e5a8845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{162.5}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507057} {:answer/id #uuid "fa98fec8-3523-5533-9521-2d921e141db4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{153}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507228}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2599c014-0b03-5502-8a02-0d8a8d6a630b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{157.5}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506762} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d5b2c85-00d9-5d4d-b67d-cda4b8c7f931" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507285}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4519e899-8275-5799-805c-1511d6914420" :question/math-academy-id "q-67893" :question/problem "What is the measure of each interior angle of a regular polygon with $16$ sides?" :question/worked-solution "A regular polygon with $16$ sides has all its interior angles with the same measure.\n\nThe sum of the measures of its interior angles is \n\n$$\n{180}^{∘}\\times (16-2)=2\\,{520}^{∘}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the measure of each interior angle is \n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\,{520}^{∘}}{16}={157.5}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507469 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105698 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5231e20f-0e57-517c-bae9-3a152234d5ab" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Exterior Angles of a Regular Polygon"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e02d0b3-b302-5cb6-9286-334dfa499923" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 175921